                        <field name="dc_description">This volume of registers from the faculty of arts contains, as its oldest and originally sepa-rate part, the statutes of the faculty. At the end of the 15th century, they were bound toge-ther with an academic calendar and with two registers containing the names of students and graduates (‘baccalaureates’) matriculated since 1461. Quires originally left blank for this purpose continue the list of degrees (‘magister’ and ‘baccalaureate’) awarded until 1848. </field>
